<section class="sec" id="pricing">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div style="text-align:center;max-width:800px;margin:0 auto">
      <p class="eyebrow">Fair &amp; Regulated Terms</p>
      <h1>Clear, Transparent Pricing</h1>
      <p class="lede">The contingency fee is due only after an approved, paid claim. Review the administrative and document charges below before starting.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fees-container" style="max-width:900px;margin:var(--sp3) auto 0;width:100%">
      <div>
        <h2 class="fees-title" style="text-align:left">What will it cost to process my claim?</h2>
        <p class="fees-intro" style="margin-top:12px">
          The contingency fee is limited by federal rules. <strong>We do not collect that contingency fee until your claim has been approved and paid.</strong> Separate administrative charges are listed below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="fees-list">
        <li>
          <strong>New Claims:</strong> For new RECA claims, our fee is <strong>2%</strong> of the total compensation awarded.<br>
          <em>Example: For a Downwinder claim awarded $100,000, our fee is $2,000.</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Resubmitted Claims:</strong> If we are resubmitting a previously denied claim, the fee is <strong>10%</strong> of the compensation awarded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Administrative Fees:</strong>
          <ul class="fees-sublist">
            <li>A non-refundable <strong>$200 file review fee</strong> is charged upfront. This covers administrative services such as postage, phone calls, and initial claim processing support.</li>
            <li>A <strong>$400 per claimant administrative processing fee</strong> is charged to help cover costs incurred throughout the claims process. This fee is paid upon completion of the claim.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Document Retrieval Fees:</strong><br>
          We obtain necessary documentation—such as medical records, presence documents, and vital records—on your behalf. These are billed <strong>per document</strong>, but payment is not due until the claim has been processed.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout-box" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <strong>Zero Contingency Risk</strong>
        <p>If your claim is not approved and paid by the Department of Justice, you owe zero contingency fee. You will see every cost outlined in writing before you sign anything.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="btns" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <a class="btn" href="/check/">Check Your Eligibility</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Speak With A Specialist</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
